    "body": "## DUNCAN PRIME — FIRST RESULT NIGHT PREFLIGHT / RUN 05\n\n**RESULT**\n- Fresh state restored before action.\n- `main = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`.\n- `duncan/zorr-studio-r01 = f67fd9454a6c2702e60b270634d934dc2ea62665`.\n- #248 remains the active production gate; #249 remains A critical path; #250 remains downstream PREP-only; #251 remains MASTER; PR #252 remains OPEN / DRAFT / NOT MERGED at `bfd693fa563a5fba7869ee5adabe23a9d9ce5aec`.\n- OWNER W01..W06 visual authority remains durable in #248 comment `5485989573`.\n- Frozen witness protocol fresh-read confirms supplementary accepted refs are exactly:\n  - suit five-view turnaround = Library `file_0000000004f882469dfa7a8b272ac5c4`\n  - costume/accessory sheet = Library `file_0000000037b4821082deb5afcb57227e`\n\n**DELTA**\nPerformed a bounded hash-first sweep over 10 previously unchecked UUID PNGs from the Library source-era cluster around the C00 build window. All 10 were materialized as raw bytes and SHA256-computed. None matches the frozen C00 authority hashes (`94c185...`, `57fbec...`, `49f1c5...`) or provides a proven replacement for the two exact accepted Library refs.\n\nFreshly excluded candidates:\n- `c93a92d8-af72-43e0-8987-cb759099d56c.png` -> `17abc5252e7f41a6f4dcfaff84ddedbbaad712a76a53688e78e7cfa65310dc88`\n- `3536e802-64fe-4cfe-b363-6aa08f21490a.png` -> `c2a8407faad8a9420b907066452986e03f3af17695b7ceb7e9fcbfe7dac11216`\n- `81750703-50fe-45cc-acae-879a13b31c75.png` -> `c1fe8cc8fe17ca91b713feab3a7c4f8f7e7bb2b147698f34ebdeb5ae0d4f87b6`\n- `bdd0aa4c-baa7-465e-bbb0-6c1e1520931b.png` -> `e4e113a5be8e59583b577deb835e134feac9964a78d0679bb014179b9de2bf94`\n- `4d0a0f09-8a8f-4460-aa4a-12e0331ad212.png` -> `a5bf2cf8e2a96cdecacff0e097dc32a44ed7356d53b27c7e2c7b2ed99c3f958f`\n- `ae2ae249-8419-47a0-a6cc-8e46599929b0.png` -> `9f31935946de0559a4c74b9c35b463125caa54df1438b4406eccb47f8b58c905`\n- `24fccd3b-2617-4e05-9b31-4c81dded736a.png` -> `8e97cad48fb215600d694560b9f1438042281448f8b7c739ba081d792d242eae`\n- `a5f3bfbd-6924-4110-a2db-9715a2c65490.png` -> `7b7af3424b08e7ec6c13fafe405275cf83fc2da6164a431dccf708a165aeb699`\n- `55d55a04-ce2f-42d5-84dc-f3f12c680417.png` -> `92d285b180088fb50b13c8e260d205cc15adf5865af7cf9ee61eaa71cce36e6c`\n- `32391623-606e-461e-bd1f-68c03e838831.png` -> `4cb81aeb857d426f51899096baafec1775f38a5021aef5d1cf6057eb7636d968`\n\n**EVIDENCE**\n- Exact protocol at current studio HEAD still names the two accepted Library IDs above; no substitution law exists.\n- Library metadata/source-era cluster is physically visible, but the two exact accepted file IDs are still not returned as visible/materializable handles in this runtime.\n- No image generation/editing surface is exposed in this run, so no W01 witness was fabricated.\n\n**OPEN**\n- `EXACT_ACCEPTED_SUIT_TURNAROUND_HANDLE = NOT VISIBLE`\n- `EXACT_ACCEPTED_COSTUME_ACCESSORY_HANDLE = NOT VISIBLE`\n- `SOURCE_BYTES_FOR_EXACT_ACCEPTED_REFS = NOT MATERIALIZED`\n- `W01 = NOT EXECUTED`\n- `COSTUME_MECHANICS_R01 != PASS`\n\n**NEXT**\nContinue hash-first recovery only: resolve/materialize the two exact accepted Library refs (or prove their exact bytes through a durable source-pack mapping), fresh-verify source authority, then execute **W01 only** when a real visual execution surface is present. Do not substitute visually similar files, do not generate a replacement source, and do not open downstream gates.",
